{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "metadata": {
    "id": "murmur-demo-bell-attack",
    "name": "DEMO: BELL ATTACK TRANSIENT",
    "author": "Patchwork Eight Engineering",
    "description": "Modulation demo: a second, independent envelope shaping ONE operator's presence over time, separate from the main amp envelope -- the classic FM/bell 'bright transient over a sustained tone' trick. Node 0 (triangle, ratio 1.0) is a plain sustained tone under Envelope 1 (the amp envelope) as usual. Node 1 (square, ratio 3.01, deliberately inharmonic) sits at a near-silent base level (0.04) but is routed Envelope 2 -> Operator Level (targetIndex 1, amount 18): OperatorLevel modulation is multiplicative (level *= 1 + sourceValue * amount, ModMatrixExecutor.hpp), so at Envelope 2's near-instant attack peak the node briefly reaches ~0.76 effective level, then Envelope 2's fast decay to a zero sustain drops it back to near-silent for the rest of the note -- a bright inharmonic 'ping' at the front of an otherwise plain tone, entirely from a second envelope most patches never use as anything but a spare.",
    "category": "keys",
    "moods": [
      "modulation-demo",
      "bell",
      "percussive-attack"
    ],
    "genres": [
      "demo"
    ],
